BT 1 0 0 1 0 39 Tm /F1 9 Tf 12 TL (A flat if\226elif chain is clearest because the slabs are ordered and exclusive. Nested if statements can obscure the complete) Tj T* (rule; combined Boolean expressions are concise when parenthesised. A match\226case can match guarded conditions, while) Tj T* (a list of upper-limit rules can be scanned in order. For k slabs, a chain or list scan is O\(k\) worst case and O\(1\) extra space;) Tj T* (a small fixed set of branches is effectively constant. A dictionary lookup is not ideal for continuous ranges.) Tj T* ET
